# One IOCCC entry out of the twelve in SRC/ioccc became a program on this disk;
# DOC/ORIGINS names it: `queens ... IOCCC entry by M. Baruch'.  The other
# eleven are entries nobody built and there is nothing on the disk to match.
queens|ioccc|baruch.c|||
# The six xasm cross-assemblers, all from one common core plus one do<n>.c.
# They are 6800, 6801, 6804, 6805, 6809 and 68HC11 -- NOT 68k, whatever
# DOC/INDEX used to say.  Two defects had to go first: as.h declared Page_num
# and Obj_name EXTERN while as.c also defines them (and as.c compiles with
# EXTERN empty), and do11.c alone still spelled the program counter Pc/Old_pc
# after everything else had been renamed PPC/Old_PPC.
as0|xasm|do0.c as.c util.c ffwd.c output.c pseudo.c eval.c symtab.c|||
as1|xasm|do1.c as.c util.c ffwd.c output.c pseudo.c eval.c symtab.c|||
as4|xasm|do4.c as.c util.c ffwd.c output.c pseudo.c eval.c symtab.c|||
as5|xasm|do5.c as.c util.c ffwd.c output.c pseudo.c eval.c symtab.c|||
as9|xasm|do9.c as.c util.c ffwd.c output.c pseudo.c eval.c symtab.c|||
as11|xasm|do11.c as.c util.c ffwd.c output.c pseudo.c eval.c symtab.c|||
